WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:20.562
I'm sorry about this.

2
00:00:20.646 --> 00:00:24.900
Don't you dare apologize. Thanks to you,
we can afford to get the other car fixed.

3
00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.235
Tell him, boys.

4
00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:27.277
-Bye, Dad.
-It's all right, Dad.

5
00:00:27.361 --> 00:00:28.237
Whatever.

6
00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:31.657
-Love you.
-Love you, darling.

7
00:00:32.448 --> 00:00:35.536
And tell your boss
I hope she gets heart disease.

8
00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.706
-Morning, Ted.
-Hey, Higgins--

9
00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:42.835
Is he dead?

10
00:00:44.962 --> 00:00:48.048
I mean, you know, it's my fault
for staring at my phone.

11
00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:50.133
I just can't stop
checking on my family's flight.

12
00:00:50.217 --> 00:00:51.969
You know, I haven't shared this
with too many folks,

13
00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:55.681
but Michelle and I,
we've been having some marital issues.

14
00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:58.725
Ted, you really don't have to
talk about this if you don't want to.

15
00:00:58.809 --> 00:00:59.726
I don't mind.

16
00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:01.937
Tried couples therapy.

17
00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.647
Didn't like the other couple though.

18
00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.026
It feels good to laugh.

19
00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.988
Yeah, you know, our therapist
gave us this code word to use.

20
00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.115
So if either of us says "Oklahoma,"

21
00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:15.409
the other one has to tell
the God's honest truth.

22
00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:17.369
Yeah, you know, it's pretty helpful.

23
00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:19.329
Did ruin the musical for me though.

24
00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:22.124
So now every time I hear,
"Oh, What a Beautiful Mornin',"

25
00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:26.295
or... what--
"Surrey with the Fringe on Top," or--

26
00:01:26.795 --> 00:01:28.964
-"Shall We Dance?"
-No, that's from <i>King and I</i>.

27
00:01:29.673 --> 00:01:31.717
Anyway, if I hear any of those tunes,

28
00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.635
I immediately think about
my wife telling me

29
00:01:33.719 --> 00:01:37.014
that my constant optimism is too much.

30
00:01:38.182 --> 00:01:41.185
And this... sharing of feelings

31
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.646
is 'cause I opened up to you
about my ex-husband at the gala.

32
00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.064
Yes, ma'am.

33
00:01:46.148 --> 00:01:47.524
Well, that's a lesson learned.

34
00:01:47.608 --> 00:01:48.775
Come on now.

35
00:01:48.859 --> 00:01:51.653
I bet deep down you kinda dig
we're getting so close, right?

36
00:01:51.737 --> 00:01:52.863
I do.

37
00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.948
-Oklahoma?
-I do not.

38
00:02:18.263 --> 00:02:19.348
Jamie?

39
00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:21.808
You up?

40
00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:29.358
Hello?

41
00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:31.777
Is Jamie here?

42
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.820
Oh, my God. You're Keeley Jones.

43
00:02:33.904 --> 00:02:35.572
Yeah, I am.

44
00:02:37.449 --> 00:02:38.450
Hi, Jamie.

45
00:02:40.327 --> 00:02:42.996
No, no. No. You can't get mad.
You broke up with me.

46
00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.623
Like, 24 hours ago.

47
00:02:44.706 --> 00:02:46.166
How long's a man meant to be alone?

48
00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.085
What am I supposed to do?
Shower by myself?

49
00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:51.004
Sorry, can I just say,
I'm your biggest fan.

50
00:02:51.088 --> 00:02:53.006
I follow your Insta,
your Snap, everything.

51
00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:55.008
Wow, thank you.

52
00:02:55.509 --> 00:02:56.844
And, Jamie, thank you.

53
00:02:57.261 --> 00:03:00.806
Whenever I break up with someone,
I spend months questioning it,

54
00:03:00.889 --> 00:03:03.350
wondering if I made
a huge fucking mistake.

55
00:03:03.433 --> 00:03:07.312
But you have really helped me to feel good
about this decision, just by...

56
00:03:10.107 --> 00:03:11.275
being you.

57
00:03:11.775 --> 00:03:12.776
You're welcome.

58
00:03:13.402 --> 00:03:14.444
What?

59
00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:16.363
You said I made you feel good
about your decision.

60
00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.532
-Yeah.
-Did you mean it?

61
00:03:19.867 --> 00:03:21.702
-Yes.
-Well, then you're welcome.

62
00:03:22.703 --> 00:03:24.121
I like to make people feel good.

63
00:03:26.248 --> 00:03:28.208
You still gonna be around
for the promo shoot later?

64
00:03:28.292 --> 00:03:30.794
The promo shoot
that I've spent weeks setting up for you?

65
00:03:31.545 --> 00:03:32.504
Yes.

66
00:03:34.923 --> 00:03:36.592
It was nice to meet you.

67
00:03:42.014 --> 00:03:43.223
Yes, yes, yes! Here!

68
00:03:44.641 --> 00:03:46.185
Yes, Jamie! Jamie, Jamie!

69
00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:49.146
Jamie, I'm open. Jamie!

70
00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:53.525
-What are you doing? That was going in.
-Well, we'll never know.

71
00:03:53.609 --> 00:03:55.903
Jamie, how many times I gotta tell you
to make the extra pass?

72
00:03:55.986 --> 00:03:59.698
Come on. Sam was more open than the jar
of peanut butter on my kitchen counter.

73
00:03:59.781 --> 00:04:01.825
What? What's he talking about?

74
00:04:01.909 --> 00:04:04.369
That's right. Y'all don't know
I like to keep the peanut butter open.

75
00:04:04.453 --> 00:04:06.872
That way, whenever I walk by,
I can just stick my finger in there.

76
00:04:07.998 --> 00:04:10.167
-It's a fucking good idea, to be fair.
-Yeah, it is.

77
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.961
Now look, when Sam is that open,
you gotta pass to him, okay?

78
00:04:13.045 --> 00:04:16.255
But why?
Even when Sam's open, Sam is still shit.

79
00:04:16.339 --> 00:04:17.925
I heard my name. What did he say?

80
00:04:18.007 --> 00:04:19.760
-Don't worry about it.
-Okay.

81
00:04:19.843 --> 00:04:21.470
Guys, we gotta play like a team tomorrow.

82
00:04:21.553 --> 00:04:24.973
Otherwise we're gonna
get our butts kicked. Extra passes.

83
00:04:25.057 --> 00:04:27.684
We're gonna keep doing this
until we get it right. Let's go.

84
00:04:27.768 --> 00:04:29.019
Dad!

85
00:04:34.233 --> 00:04:35.484
Practice is canceled.

86
00:04:39.446 --> 00:04:41.990
That is a lot longer run
than he thinks, though.

87
00:04:42.074 --> 00:04:43.075
Metaphor.

88
00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.120
-Hey!
-Daddy!

89
00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:49.665
I kinda thought y'all would meet me
halfway, but hey, that's all right.

90
00:04:49.748 --> 00:04:51.708
-Hey, buddy!
-Helicopter!

91
00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:55.879
You got it. Two spins. How about that?

92
00:04:55.963 --> 00:04:57.506
Boy, you're gonna be a dizzy fella there.

93
00:04:57.589 --> 00:04:59.967
-Slower helicopter.
-No way. Come on now.

94
00:05:03.637 --> 00:05:04.847
I missed you so much.

95
00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.306
Group hug.

96
00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:07.641
Hey! There he is.

97
00:05:07.724 --> 00:05:11.228
Hey, big guy. Look how tall you got.
What the heck?

98
00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.730
And look at this. I mean, you, what--
You got teeth now?

99
00:05:13.814 --> 00:05:16.149
-I already had teeth!
-And you can talk!

100
00:05:16.233 --> 00:05:18.068
Also, Ms. Welton, sorry to report,

101
00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:22.197
but this weekend's match
will not be completely sold out.

102
00:05:22.281 --> 00:05:25.742
Not a surprise. We've lost four matches
in a row, and we're facing relegation.

103
00:05:26.368 --> 00:05:27.828
But why be sorry?

104
00:05:27.911 --> 00:05:29.746
I think it's all going rather smashingly.

105
00:05:34.251 --> 00:05:38.672
I'm happy to be the new brand ambassador
for Darsteiner.

106
00:05:38.755 --> 00:05:41.300
The favorite beer of Jamie Tartt.

107
00:05:41.925 --> 00:05:44.261
Wait, wait, wait. Get my tats.

108
00:05:44.887 --> 00:05:48.098
Get that one. It's very important to me.
Chinese for "arm."

109
00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:50.893
-Jamie.
-What?

110
00:05:50.976 --> 00:05:52.394
-Just drink the beer.
-Yeah.

111
00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.939
No judgment,
but are you back with that twat?

112
00:05:56.023 --> 00:05:57.149
<i>Bon appétit</i>.

113
00:05:57.733 --> 00:06:00.903
No. We're done.
God, I love that you care though.

114
00:06:01.528 --> 00:06:03.739
I'll kiss you on the mouth
if I can reach those lips.

115
00:06:04.448 --> 00:06:06.992
You know, I put this whole thing together.
I get 10%.

116
00:06:07.075 --> 00:06:08.619
Hey, do you like mythology?

117
00:06:08.702 --> 00:06:10.954
You've seen a unicorn.
You ever seen a brewnicorn?

118
00:06:13.415 --> 00:06:15.542
-That's fucking funny.
-Oh, no.

119
00:06:15.626 --> 00:06:17.628
What's that? It's my beerby.

120
00:06:17.711 --> 00:06:19.046
-Come on.
-Okay.

121
00:06:19.129 --> 00:06:22.007
Y'all getting all this for free.
Not even extra for that.

122
00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.091
Keeley.

123
00:06:23.175 --> 00:06:26.178
If any of the other players
needed some branding work done,

124
00:06:26.261 --> 00:06:28.305
is that something you'd be interested in?

125
00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:29.515
I don't want you to offer me a job

126
00:06:29.598 --> 00:06:31.475
just 'cause I was nice to you
in the loo the other night.

127
00:06:31.558 --> 00:06:35.103
Why not? Men give each other jobs
in toilets all the time.

128
00:06:35.979 --> 00:06:36.980
Yeah, they do.

129
00:06:37.814 --> 00:06:40.567
I meant employment. Like job-jobs.

130
00:06:40.651 --> 00:06:43.320
-So not hand, or blow, or foot?
-Foot?

131
00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:47.491
You're right.
Technically it would be... feet, right?

132
00:06:48.659 --> 00:06:52.120
Just give it a thought.
Unless you want to carry on doing--

133
00:06:52.788 --> 00:06:53.997
What is it you do again?

134
00:06:54.957 --> 00:06:57.835
I'm sort of famous
for being almost famous.

135
00:06:58.544 --> 00:06:59.545
Excellent.

136
00:07:00.796 --> 00:07:03.173
-Maybe think of it as a plan B.
-Yeah.

137
00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:07.386
Okay, now,
little tip for y'all, all right?

138
00:07:07.469 --> 00:07:10.931
Fries are called "chips."
Chips are called "crisps."

139
00:07:11.014 --> 00:07:13.433
And "bangers" aren't great songs,

140
00:07:13.517 --> 00:07:16.645
but they do make you feel like dancing
'cause they're so darn tasty.

141
00:07:16.728 --> 00:07:19.189
When you gonna win a game,
you fucking wanker?

142
00:07:19.273 --> 00:07:22.401
Hey, Baz. Fellas.
This here-- This is my wife, Michelle.

143
00:07:22.484 --> 00:07:24.611
Absolute pleasure to meet you, Mrs. Lasso.

144
00:07:24.695 --> 00:07:26.738
Nice recovery. Well executed.

145
00:07:26.822 --> 00:07:28.532
-Yeah, coach's wife. She's heard it all.
-Yeah.

146
00:07:28.615 --> 00:07:30.701
Hi, Ted. Hello, young man.

147
00:07:31.493 --> 00:07:36.248
Here are the darts. There's the board.
Try not to hit any regulars.

148
00:07:37.082 --> 00:07:38.250
Yeah, go have fun.

149
00:07:38.333 --> 00:07:40.752
-Your table's this way.
-Go on. After you.

150
00:07:40.836 --> 00:07:43.297
-Three fish-and-chips?
-Yes, please. And two pints.

151
00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:45.007
-I like your style.
-Yeah.

152
00:07:47.926 --> 00:07:49.178
Look at this.

153
00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:55.726
Do they wrap the fish-and-chips
in newspaper? I read they do that here.

154
00:07:55.809 --> 00:07:59.438
No, no. I wish. Boy, I'd love that.
Having my food teach me stuff?

155
00:07:59.521 --> 00:08:01.440
Yeah, that's your dream scenario, right?

156
00:08:01.523 --> 00:08:03.567
A doughnut
that knows about Rosa Parks or something.

157
00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:05.360
-Yeah. Exactly, yeah.
-Yeah.

158
00:08:05.444 --> 00:08:07.654
Can fit a lot of wisdom just in the hole.

159
00:08:09.281 --> 00:08:10.324
Yeah.

160
00:08:10.782 --> 00:08:12.492
You already done, bud?

161
00:08:12.576 --> 00:08:14.286
Yeah, he probably should be.

162
00:08:14.369 --> 00:08:16.496
Well, I'm sorry about that.

163
00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:17.748
Happens all the time.

164
00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.085
-What are you doing?
-I'm just curious, yeah?

165
00:08:22.169 --> 00:08:24.087
The photographer's gonna
send me over the pictures,

166
00:08:24.171 --> 00:08:26.048
and I'll just kill the ones
where you look like shit.

167
00:08:26.131 --> 00:08:27.299
Then I'll send them over to you.

168
00:08:27.382 --> 00:08:30.594
Firstly, babe, there won't be any
where I look like shit because...

169
00:08:31.595 --> 00:08:34.640
And B, why don't you just
bring them over to my place

170
00:08:34.722 --> 00:08:36.433
and we can look at them together?

171
00:08:36.933 --> 00:08:38.059
Maybe we're naked.

172
00:08:40.145 --> 00:08:42.481
Hard no. Thank you again, Jamie.

173
00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:46.318
Smart move.

174
00:08:47.486 --> 00:08:48.487
Excuse me?

175
00:08:50.322 --> 00:08:52.199
I have to hang out with that prick.

176
00:08:52.282 --> 00:08:55.494
The fact that you would choose
to be with him is frankly mind-blowing.

177
00:08:55.577 --> 00:08:57.371
I'm not with him. We broke up.

178
00:08:57.454 --> 00:09:00.374
We're working together, actually.
And who asked you anyway, huh?

179
00:09:00.457 --> 00:09:01.458
Right.

180
00:09:02.668 --> 00:09:05.379
I didn't know that, so... apologies.

181
00:09:05.462 --> 00:09:08.131
No, it's fine.
You should definitely weigh in on my life.

182
00:09:08.215 --> 00:09:11.969
I'll make sure that I text you
anytime I have to make a decision, yeah?

183
00:09:14.429 --> 00:09:16.890
It's just that in training,
Sam was wide open,

184
00:09:16.974 --> 00:09:18.600
and Jamie wouldn't pass to him.

185
00:09:18.684 --> 00:09:20.227
But Sam was wide open.

186
00:09:20.727 --> 00:09:22.479
Now that's what I'm dealing with.

187
00:09:28.819 --> 00:09:29.820
Yes.

188
00:09:31.572 --> 00:09:32.614
Here it is.

189
00:09:33.198 --> 00:09:36.159
Yeah. Okay. Now, hold on a second.

190
00:09:37.536 --> 00:09:40.330
Think we might have missed a page.
Oh, boy.

191
00:09:40.414 --> 00:09:42.958
Don't you wanna go
ride a real double-decker bus?

192
00:09:43.041 --> 00:09:44.626
After we finish.

193
00:09:45.335 --> 00:09:46.670
See? I like that.

194
00:09:46.753 --> 00:09:48.881
First we gotta build it,
then we can ride it.

195
00:09:48.964 --> 00:09:51.633
It's kind of a <i>Field of Dreams</i> paradigm.

196
00:09:52.092 --> 00:09:53.093
Okay.

197
00:09:53.886 --> 00:09:57.139
Well, six hands are better than four.

198
00:10:25.959 --> 00:10:27.669
Good morning.

199
00:10:27.753 --> 00:10:29.046
Hey, how you doing?

200
00:10:32.382 --> 00:10:35.302
-Hey, look at that scarf. I like it.
-Oi! Wanker.

201
00:10:35.385 --> 00:10:37.221
Don't you fuck up the match.

202
00:10:37.304 --> 00:10:39.723
I appreciate you.
We'll see what happens, huh?

203
00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.187
Hey, check it out.

204
00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:47.231
You never--
Never seen one of these before.

205
00:10:47.314 --> 00:10:49.942
That right there, that's a scone, okay?

206
00:10:50.025 --> 00:10:52.277
It's like a muffin, except
it sucks all the spit out of your mouth.

207
00:10:52.361 --> 00:10:54.571
There's your breakfast. All right?
Hey! What do you say?

208
00:10:54.655 --> 00:10:55.948
Thanks, Dad!

209
00:10:56.031 --> 00:10:58.742
Okay. There you go.
Some people's kids, holy moly.

210
00:11:05.666 --> 00:11:09.169
-It's pretty nice out there, isn't it?
-Yeah.

211
00:11:09.253 --> 00:11:10.879
-Hey.
-I can make us some breakfast.

212
00:11:10.963 --> 00:11:12.130
What's wrong?

213
00:11:12.214 --> 00:11:14.383
Nothing. I think I'm just
a little jet-lagged is all.

214
00:11:14.466 --> 00:11:15.634
I'm fine, Ted.

215
00:11:15.717 --> 00:11:17.553
No, no. No.
Michelle, you gotta talk to me.

216
00:11:17.636 --> 00:11:20.138
Okay? Hey, hey. Oklahoma.

217
00:11:26.395 --> 00:11:27.646
Every day...

218
00:11:29.106 --> 00:11:33.110
I wake up hoping that
I'll feel the way I felt in the beginning.

219
00:11:33.986 --> 00:11:37.239
But maybe that's
just what marriage is, right?

220
00:11:38.699 --> 00:11:41.577
I'll keep trying. You know I will.

221
00:11:43.537 --> 00:11:45.163
Ready to go!

222
00:11:49.042 --> 00:11:51.044
-I mean, you're gonna need pants, kiddo.
-Yeah.

223
00:11:51.128 --> 00:11:53.046
-You know--
-Let's get some pants. Come on.

224
00:12:03.223 --> 00:12:05.225
I mean, I don't know
what I'm supposed to do.

225
00:12:05.851 --> 00:12:08.312
Marriage.
Just so, you know, so complicated.

226
00:12:08.395 --> 00:12:10.314
So many different challenges and...

227
00:12:10.898 --> 00:12:13.567
I think-- I don't know. Sorry.

228
00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:14.860
You ever been married?

229
00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:19.448
Yeah, Nate.
Coach's views on romantic relationships

230
00:12:19.531 --> 00:12:21.909
are not too dissimilar
from his views on cooking steak.

231
00:12:21.992 --> 00:12:25.370
You know, you spend any more than
five minutes on one, loses its flavor.

232
00:12:25.454 --> 00:12:27.706
-That sound about right, Coach?
-Yeah.

233
00:12:27.789 --> 00:12:29.791
Do you mind
if I ask you a personal question then?

234
00:12:29.875 --> 00:12:30.792
Fire away.

235
00:12:30.876 --> 00:12:32.211
If you were worried
about your relationship,

236
00:12:32.294 --> 00:12:36.089
then why did you fly 4,438 miles away?

237
00:12:36.173 --> 00:12:38.759
That is a very specific number
to know off the top of your head.

238
00:12:38.842 --> 00:12:40.719
Well, my dad used to be a cartographer.

239
00:12:41.178 --> 00:12:44.473
Used to say I was .001 miles tall.

240
00:12:46.391 --> 00:12:49.520
Yeah. Well, it's a good question.
Why do it?

241
00:12:51.104 --> 00:12:52.689
I think at some point I realized

242
00:12:52.773 --> 00:12:57.486
that me being around so much
was doing more harm than good.

243
00:12:59.363 --> 00:13:02.199
Like, anytime I tried
to solve any of her problems, or...

244
00:13:03.909 --> 00:13:07.162
do something sweet for her,
it just would backfire.

245
00:13:08.121 --> 00:13:11.250
And then she and this therapist
we were working with

246
00:13:11.333 --> 00:13:15.796
decided that maybe the best thing to do
would be to give her a little space.

247
00:13:15.879 --> 00:13:20.759
And so... well, I gave her 4,400 and...

248
00:13:20.843 --> 00:13:21.677
Thirty-eight.

249
00:13:22.594 --> 00:13:24.179
Thirty-eight miles worth of it.

250
00:13:26.557 --> 00:13:29.685
Sorry to interrupt.
I was told one of you had my phone.

251
00:13:31.186 --> 00:13:32.312
Thank heavens.

252
00:13:32.396 --> 00:13:34.731
I deleted some apps
to optimize performance.

253
00:13:34.815 --> 00:13:36.358
Not Battleships, I hope.

254
00:13:36.441 --> 00:13:38.569
Oh, well.
I was playing that too much anyway.

255
00:13:38.652 --> 00:13:41.321
I'll leave you lads
to your match day planning.

256
00:13:41.405 --> 00:13:43.282
Now, well, hold your horse there, amigo.

257
00:13:43.365 --> 00:13:45.158
You mind if I get your take on something?

258
00:13:45.242 --> 00:13:47.286
Wow, of course.

259
00:13:47.369 --> 00:13:52.040
Very exciting to be invited
into the inner sanctum.

260
00:13:52.791 --> 00:13:55.210
Team Lasso, as it were.

261
00:13:55.294 --> 00:13:57.588
You and the missus.
Y'all been together a while, yeah?

262
00:13:58.005 --> 00:14:01.175
Yes, 28 years.

263
00:14:01.258 --> 00:14:03.468
Five boys, three dogs,

264
00:14:03.552 --> 00:14:07.389
one 20-year-old cat whose impending death
will wreck me emotionally,

265
00:14:07.472 --> 00:14:10.601
and one small house
that manages to fit us all in it.

266
00:14:11.059 --> 00:14:12.686
Sounds like a full life right there.

267
00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:16.523
But I assume y'all have had your
fair share of hard times though, yeah?

268
00:14:16.607 --> 00:14:20.861
Did you not hear the five boys,
tiny house, dying cat part?

269
00:14:23.739 --> 00:14:24.907
That's the thing though, isn't it?

270
00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.952
If you're with the right person,
even the hard times are easy.

271
00:14:31.955 --> 00:14:36.084
Someone call 911.
I want to report a truth bomb.

272
00:14:37.127 --> 00:14:40.005
-I think they do 999 here.
-It is 999.

273
00:14:40.088 --> 00:14:41.340
-Yes. It is, yeah.
-For emergencies?

274
00:14:41.423 --> 00:14:43.008
Boy, that seems troublesome to me.

275
00:14:43.091 --> 00:14:45.427
You know,
toddlers and, just, butt dials and--

276
00:14:45.511 --> 00:14:46.637
-'Cause it's one key.
-Yeah.

277
00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.639
You'd probably have
police cars and ambulances

278
00:14:48.722 --> 00:14:50.599
-just zipping all over the place.
-Yeah.

279
00:14:50.682 --> 00:14:52.559
-Well, that happens a lot, doesn't it?
-It does. Yeah, yeah.

280
00:14:52.643 --> 00:14:54.686
-That explains it, actually.
-There you have it.

281
00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:56.980
<i>Arlo White here with Chris Powell.</i>

282
00:14:57.064 --> 00:15:00.567
Live from Nelson Road Stadium,
the home of AFC Richmond.

283
00:15:00.651 --> 00:15:02.277
All right, everyone!
Get in a fucking circle.

284
00:15:02.361 --> 00:15:04.029
-Let's throw this down!
-Come on, boys!

285
00:15:04.112 --> 00:15:05.572
Right, hands in.

286
00:15:05.656 --> 00:15:07.908
On three. One, two, three...

287
00:15:07.991 --> 00:15:09.993
-Richmond!
-Let's go!

288
00:15:13.455 --> 00:15:15.249
Let's go! Let's go!

289
00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:23.382
Jamie, you a germophobe?

290
00:15:23.465 --> 00:15:25.467
'Cause I'm trying to think of a reason
you didn't put your hand in

291
00:15:25.551 --> 00:15:26.468
with the rest of the team.

292
00:15:26.552 --> 00:15:27.594
Didn't want to.

293
00:15:29.638 --> 00:15:32.641
I gotta say, man, sometimes you remind me
of my grandma with the channel hopper.

294
00:15:32.724 --> 00:15:34.226
You just push all the wrong buttons.

295
00:15:34.726 --> 00:15:39.147
Well, then how's about
you and me make a deal?

296
00:15:39.231 --> 00:15:40.607
Okay, I'm listening.

297
00:15:40.691 --> 00:15:44.570
You get to keep on preaching
all of your yeehaw bullshit,

298
00:15:44.653 --> 00:15:49.825
and in exchange, I'll keep ignoring you,
because this team is tragic.

299
00:15:51.243 --> 00:15:54.246
I score all the goals,
and I'm the only one they come to see.

300
00:15:54.997 --> 00:15:56.832
Does that sound fair? Hands in.

301
00:15:57.708 --> 00:15:59.585
You know, I'd love to hash out
some of the nuances there,

302
00:15:59.668 --> 00:16:01.044
but I'm not having the best of days--

303
00:16:01.128 --> 00:16:02.546
Actually, it doesn't matter what you say.

304
00:16:02.629 --> 00:16:05.340
'Cause in my head, I'm just
hearing the crowd cheer my name

305
00:16:05.424 --> 00:16:06.842
after I score a goal tonight.

306
00:16:07.301 --> 00:16:12.264
<i>Jamie Tartt...
Jamie Tartt...</i>

307
00:16:12.347 --> 00:16:15.309
As undeniably catchy as that tune is,
I need you to cut the crap right now--

308
00:16:15.392 --> 00:16:16.768
Dad!

309
00:16:16.852 --> 00:16:20.022
Hey, big guy. There he is. Hey.

310
00:16:20.105 --> 00:16:22.733
-Jamie Tartt?
-Hello, little lad.

311
00:16:22.816 --> 00:16:24.359
Would you sign my shirt?

312
00:16:25.235 --> 00:16:26.486
All right, turn around.

313
00:16:27.905 --> 00:16:28.989
That's pretty cool, huh?

314
00:16:29.698 --> 00:16:33.368
Now, next time I score a goal,
it won't just be for me.

315
00:16:36.079 --> 00:16:37.331
It'll be for you too.

316
00:16:38.916 --> 00:16:42.252
And for me. But... just for us.

317
00:16:42.836 --> 00:16:44.588
-Cool.
-Good lad.

318
00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:47.716
Good boy.

319
00:16:50.135 --> 00:16:51.720
Come on, let's get out there.

320
00:16:51.803 --> 00:16:57.267
<i>Jamie Tartt...
Jamie Tartt...</i>

321
00:16:57.351 --> 00:16:58.810
-Come on, goalie!
-<i>Link finds space.</i>

322
00:16:58.894 --> 00:17:00.229
<i>He rears back to shoot it.</i>

323
00:17:00.312 --> 00:17:02.731
<i>A stunning goal
by the Canadian midfielder!</i>

324
00:17:02.814 --> 00:17:06.777
-Fuck's sake!
-I hate that poxy wanker! Fucking Lasso!

325
00:17:06.859 --> 00:17:10.030
-Nice family though.
-Damn it, Paul! Don't humanize him!

326
00:17:10.113 --> 00:17:13.575
Well, after only six minutes,
Richmond are 2-0 down.

327
00:17:13.659 --> 00:17:14.492
Wanker! Wanker!

328
00:17:14.576 --> 00:17:16.994
<i>And the Richmond supporters
are making their feelings known.</i>

329
00:17:17.079 --> 00:17:18.079
Wanker! Wanker!

330
00:17:18.163 --> 00:17:20.082
<i>Chris, you have to think,
if this continues,</i>

331
00:17:20.165 --> 00:17:23.669
<i>Lasso's time with Richmond will be short
and not very sweet.</i>

332
00:17:24.127 --> 00:17:26.088
<i>Tartt receives the ball. Clever there.</i>

333
00:17:26.171 --> 00:17:27.798
-Go on, Jamie.
-<i>He finds space.</i>

334
00:17:27.881 --> 00:17:29.174
<i>He has Obisanya on the right.</i>

335
00:17:29.258 --> 00:17:32.970
<i>No, he's doing it himself.
And what a finish!</i>

336
00:17:33.053 --> 00:17:35.681
<i>Jamie Tartt with an incredible solo goal!</i>

337
00:17:35.764 --> 00:17:37.891
Jamie Tartt, you fucking king!

338
00:17:37.975 --> 00:17:42.229
<i>Jamie Tartt...
Jamie Tartt...</i>

339
00:17:42.312 --> 00:17:45.232
<i>And thanks to budding superstar,
Jamie Tartt,</i>

340
00:17:45.315 --> 00:17:48.819
<i>Richmond are right back in it at 2-1
in the 29th minute!</i>

341
00:17:48.902 --> 00:17:51.113
-Me!
-What's he yelling?

342
00:17:51.196 --> 00:17:55.242
"Me." He's pointing at the name
on his back and repeatedly yelling "me."

343
00:17:55.325 --> 00:17:56.827
Me!

344
00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:59.079
I thought he was saying "meat."

345
00:17:59.162 --> 00:18:01.206
But, yeah,
yours makes a lot more sense. Okay.

346
00:18:01.832 --> 00:18:04.168
-Come on!
-<i>Obisanya joins the attack.</i>

347
00:18:04.251 --> 00:18:06.920
-<i>The Nigerian is taken out!</i>
-Bullshit!

348
00:18:07.546 --> 00:18:10.465
Come on, ref! They gotta knock that off!

349
00:18:11.008 --> 00:18:13.343
<i>It'll be a yellow card here for Benson.</i>

350
00:18:13.427 --> 00:18:17.181
<i>And you have to say he got off easy there.
And Obisanya is still down.</i>

351
00:18:17.264 --> 00:18:18.765
-He might be hurt.
-Yeah.

352
00:18:18.849 --> 00:18:20.726
Excuse me, mate.

353
00:18:21.185 --> 00:18:24.438
Oi! Check on your fucking teammate.

354
00:18:25.522 --> 00:18:28.358
<i>The captain dispensing some wisdom
to the young superstar.</i>

355
00:18:28.442 --> 00:18:29.776
<i>Nothing wrong with that.</i>

356
00:18:31.153 --> 00:18:32.905
-Sam?
-Yeah?

357
00:18:32.988 --> 00:18:35.240
I'm gonna have to move you there.
There you go.

358
00:18:35.324 --> 00:18:37.826
-What is your fucking problem?
-<i>What is this?</i>

359
00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.745
<i>Kent and Tartt
are at each other's throats!</i>

360
00:18:39.828 --> 00:18:42.915
-Okay. Hey, guys! Come on! Knock it off!
-<i>Hopefully cooler heads will prevail.</i>

361
00:18:42.998 --> 00:18:44.041
Fucking kill you!

362
00:18:44.124 --> 00:18:45.083
Same team!

363
00:18:45.167 --> 00:18:48.170
-<i>Unacceptable, Arlo.</i>
-<i>Chris, have you ever struck a teammate?</i>

364
00:18:48.253 --> 00:18:50.255
-Are you mad? So what?
-<i>No, but I've wanted to.</i>

365
00:18:50.339 --> 00:18:51.465
-He's my own player.
-Yeah, yeah.

366
00:18:51.548 --> 00:18:53.509
-<i>I'm actually a bit jealous.</i>
-You gotta be--

367
00:18:53.592 --> 00:18:56.929
<i>We haven't seen this
since 2001 in Newcastle.</i>

368
00:18:57.012 --> 00:19:01.099
<i>And a season of lows for Richmond
sinks even further still.</i>

369
00:19:02.392 --> 00:19:03.602
You all right, Sam?

370
00:19:03.685 --> 00:19:05.646
Honestly, it doesn't even hurt anymore.

371
00:19:05.729 --> 00:19:08.440
But everyone was making such a fuss,
I thought I should just stay down.

372
00:19:09.566 --> 00:19:11.026
No. Listen.

373
00:19:11.109 --> 00:19:14.112
I'm gonna pull you up,
you're gonna pretend to limp very badly,

374
00:19:14.196 --> 00:19:17.157
and you're gonna gesture
like you think you can bravely go on.

375
00:19:17.741 --> 00:19:19.785
-They'll love it.
-Okay.

376
00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:24.706
<i>Obisanya is on his feet,
but can he continue?</i>

377
00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.041
Is he okay?

378
00:19:26.583 --> 00:19:28.377
<i>Looks like he'll play through the pain.</i>

379
00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:31.463
<i>Such determination. You love to see it.</i>

380
00:19:31.547 --> 00:19:32.756
Attaboy, Sam!

381
00:19:33.131 --> 00:19:37.344
<i>Tartt steps up to take the free kick,
with an opportunity to tie the game.</i>

382
00:19:37.427 --> 00:19:40.389
<i>Will he find a teammate or go for glory?</i>

383
00:19:41.014 --> 00:19:43.475
<i>With Tartt, that's usually
a rhetorical question.</i>

384
00:19:50.732 --> 00:19:52.484
<i>And he's done it!</i>

385
00:19:52.568 --> 00:19:55.737
That's two for Jamie Tartt,
and Richmond are level

386
00:19:55.821 --> 00:19:57.531
in the 38th minute!

387
00:19:57.614 --> 00:19:59.324
<i>He's a special player, Arlo.</i>

388
00:19:59.408 --> 00:20:00.409
Look at this.

389
00:20:01.243 --> 00:20:04.746
<i>And you have to wonder,
where would Richmond be without him.</i>

390
00:20:08.834 --> 00:20:09.835
I'll be right back.

391
00:20:10.794 --> 00:20:12.212
Me! Me!

392
00:20:13.547 --> 00:20:17.801
<i>We certainly haven't seen this before.
Ted Lasso is running into the stands.</i>

393
00:20:17.885 --> 00:20:19.803
Well, where the hell is he off to?

394
00:20:21.013 --> 00:20:22.764
<i>He's not slowing down on those steps.</i>

395
00:20:22.848 --> 00:20:25.601
That's some real impressive cardio
from Ted Lasso there.

396
00:20:25.684 --> 00:20:26.685
<i>Is he okay?</i>

397
00:20:28.562 --> 00:20:30.480
-Hey, Rebecca.
-Hello, Ted.

398
00:20:30.564 --> 00:20:32.524
-You're doing great, Dad.
-Yeah, you got this.

399
00:20:32.608 --> 00:20:33.609
Thanks, guys.

400
00:20:33.692 --> 00:20:35.152
I wanna bench Jamie.

401
00:20:35.944 --> 00:20:38.071
But I didn't wanna do it
without checking with you first.

402
00:20:39.031 --> 00:20:40.866
But, Ted, you're the manager.

403
00:20:40.949 --> 00:20:43.952
So whatever you decide,
you have my full support.

404
00:20:44.411 --> 00:20:46.163
Thanks, boss. All right.
Later, alligators.

405
00:20:46.246 --> 00:20:47.289
Bye, Dad.

406
00:20:50.292 --> 00:20:54.379
<i>And it appears Coach Lasso has decided
to rejoin the match already in progress.</i>

407
00:20:54.463 --> 00:20:57.049
Roberts, warm up. You're going in.
Let's go. Come on.

408
00:20:57.132 --> 00:20:59.301
Hey, highlighter. We got ourselves a sub.

409
00:20:59.384 --> 00:21:00.886
-Sixteen's going in for nine. Okay?
-Okay.

410
00:21:00.969 --> 00:21:02.471
Appreciate you, sir. Thank you.

411
00:21:09.436 --> 00:21:10.812
Okay.

412
00:21:10.896 --> 00:21:13.732
Well, it looks like Lasso is
making an early substitution here.

413
00:21:13.815 --> 00:21:15.984
<i>He's bringing Roberts on,
and he's taking off...</i>

414
00:21:16.944 --> 00:21:18.362
<i>Jamie Tartt?</i>

415
00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:21.365
He's our best player!

416
00:21:22.407 --> 00:21:23.408
Me?

417
00:21:25.035 --> 00:21:28.247
You don't know what you're doing!
You don't know what you're doing!

418
00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:29.873
What on earth?

419
00:21:29.957 --> 00:21:32.292
<i>He's taking off his best player.</i>

420
00:21:32.376 --> 00:21:34.837
<i>And with less than a minute remaining
in the half.</i>

421
00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:36.880
-Wanker! Wanker! Wanker!
-<i>Number 16, Robbie Roberts,</i>

422
00:21:36.964 --> 00:21:38.507
<i>for number 9, Jamie Tartt.</i>

423
00:21:38.590 --> 00:21:40.467
Hey, way to play out there.
Way to get us back in.

424
00:21:40.551 --> 00:21:43.971
Shut up. Fucking stupid twat.

425
00:21:45.556 --> 00:21:48.684
<i>The referee looks at his watch,
and that's halftime.</i>

426
00:21:48.767 --> 00:21:51.603
<i>What kind of reception awaits Lasso
in his locker room?</i>

427
00:22:03.866 --> 00:22:05.617
Oi, sit down and listen.

428
00:22:12.666 --> 00:22:13.959
We got ourselves a tied game.

429
00:22:15.335 --> 00:22:16.336
Nice work.

430
00:22:18.755 --> 00:22:23.093
Fellas, we're broken. We need to change.

431
00:22:23.177 --> 00:22:25.762
And, look, I know change can be scary.

432
00:22:25.846 --> 00:22:29.766
One minute, you're playing freeze tag
out there at recess with all your buddies.

433
00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:33.228
Next thing you know,
you're getting zits, your voice gets low.

434
00:22:33.312 --> 00:22:36.607
And every time your art teacher,
Ms. Scanlon, leans over your desk

435
00:22:36.690 --> 00:22:40.194
to check and see how your project's going,
you feel all squiggly inside.

436
00:22:44.281 --> 00:22:48.535
She was a striking woman.
Not classically beautiful, but striking.

437
00:22:50.329 --> 00:22:52.080
First time I ever saw tan lines.

438
00:22:52.998 --> 00:22:54.583
Most of the time, change is a good thing.

439
00:22:55.459 --> 00:22:57.294
Now, I think that's what it's all about.

440
00:22:58.837 --> 00:23:00.339
Embracing change.

441
00:23:00.756 --> 00:23:02.257
Being brave.

442
00:23:02.341 --> 00:23:06.845
Doing whatever you have to,
so that everyone in your life...

443
00:23:08.555 --> 00:23:09.973
can move forward with theirs.

444
00:23:11.767 --> 00:23:13.018
'Cause maybe...

445
00:23:14.186 --> 00:23:16.813
it's the only way
you can truly help her be happy.

446
00:23:24.321 --> 00:23:26.406
Obviously by "her,"
I'm referring to Lady Football.

447
00:23:28.492 --> 00:23:29.868
Good save.

448
00:23:30.744 --> 00:23:33.830
Sam, we're gonna shift you to midfield
for the second half.

449
00:23:34.623 --> 00:23:37.167
And Beard's gonna walk y'all
through the rest of the changes.

450
00:23:37.251 --> 00:23:38.961
Hey, hey, hey. One last thing.

451
00:23:39.044 --> 00:23:41.421
And I want everyone's eyes on me
when I say this. Look at me.

452
00:23:51.765 --> 00:23:53.976
-Never really liked Tartt.
-We know, Roy.

453
00:23:54.059 --> 00:23:55.477
Everybody, come on.

454
00:23:56.979 --> 00:23:58.814
<i>Two minutes of added time remaining.</i>

455
00:23:58.897 --> 00:24:01.024
<i>Still level at two goals apiece.</i>

456
00:24:01.108 --> 00:24:03.610
<i>Richmond have played well,
even without Jamie Tartt.</i>

457
00:24:03.694 --> 00:24:04.695
Here we go.

458
00:24:05.237 --> 00:24:07.781
He's open. He's open. He's open.
There you go.

459
00:24:07.865 --> 00:24:10.742
<i>A through ball from Cockburn.
And Kent is off to the races!</i>

460
00:24:10.826 --> 00:24:11.702
Come on!

461
00:24:11.785 --> 00:24:13.370
<i>Kent has only one man to beat.</i>

462
00:24:13.453 --> 00:24:15.914
<i>He could take it himself,</i>

463
00:24:15.998 --> 00:24:20.544
<i>but he makes the extra pass
to a wide open Obisanya!</i>

464
00:24:23.839 --> 00:24:26.341
<i>And he buries it!</i>

465
00:24:27.634 --> 00:24:28.886
Oh, my God!

466
00:24:30.220 --> 00:24:34.933
<i>Richmond take the lead with
barely a minute of stoppage time left.</i>

467
00:24:41.773 --> 00:24:45.944
<i>Scorer for Richmond's third goal,
number 24, Sam Obisanya.</i>

468
00:24:55.037 --> 00:24:56.955
Yeah!

469
00:24:57.039 --> 00:24:59.917
-I'm so sorry! I'm just so happy!
-No, I love it! I love this energy!

470
00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.711
-Here, Coach. Take this guy from me.
-Yeah!

471
00:25:06.006 --> 00:25:07.007
That's the way you do it!

472
00:25:07.090 --> 00:25:11.261
Nicely done, gentlemen! Nicely done!
Way to do it! Yes! Yes! Yes!

473
00:25:11.970 --> 00:25:13.263
Took balls, what you did.

474
00:25:14.806 --> 00:25:17.476
That's all we got is balls, Roy.
It's all we got.

475
00:25:17.559 --> 00:25:20.562
All right! Yeah!
There you go. Way to play.

476
00:25:21.522 --> 00:25:22.731
How about that, Coach?

477
00:25:23.690 --> 00:25:24.775
You hear that, Coach?

478
00:25:25.442 --> 00:25:27.444
Wanker! Wanker!

479
00:25:27.528 --> 00:25:29.238
Well, same word, ain't it?

480
00:25:30.239 --> 00:25:31.740
Yeah, but different.

481
00:25:33.075 --> 00:25:37.287
Yeah, kinda like back in the '80s
when bad meant good, right?

482
00:25:38.038 --> 00:25:39.414
Who was president back then?

483
00:25:40.082 --> 00:25:43.293
-Ronald Reagan.
-"Ronald Reagan? The actor?"

484
00:25:43.377 --> 00:25:48.173
Oh, man. I love it when you do Doc Brown.
You walked me right into that.

485
00:25:55.472 --> 00:25:58.809
Daddy! Dad!

486
00:25:58.892 --> 00:26:00.644
Hey! There he is!

487
00:26:02.521 --> 00:26:04.314
How about that, huh? We won one.

488
00:26:04.398 --> 00:26:05.399
-Daddy?
-Yeah?

489
00:26:05.482 --> 00:26:06.817
What's a wanker?

490
00:26:07.776 --> 00:26:09.653
Well, kiddo. That is a...

491
00:26:10.404 --> 00:26:13.824
That's a man that likes to be alone
with his thoughts. Make sense?

492
00:26:13.907 --> 00:26:15.492
Let's give you a better view
of all this. Ready?

493
00:26:16.368 --> 00:26:18.120
Get up there, kiddo. Look at that.

494
00:26:18.203 --> 00:26:21.874
Wave to the people. That's it.
Let them know. Let them see, huh?

495
00:26:24.501 --> 00:26:26.253
Shit.

496
00:26:29.381 --> 00:26:30.382
Yeah.

497
00:26:31.800 --> 00:26:32.801
One touch.

498
00:26:36.638 --> 00:26:40.184
I just keep thinking about
the first time we met, back at school.

499
00:26:42.644 --> 00:26:46.440
Us being the only two people in that big
old parking lot at the exact same time.

500
00:26:48.942 --> 00:26:50.652
So random.

501
00:26:50.736 --> 00:26:53.614
No way for us to know that it was going
to be the start of something.

502
00:26:55.616 --> 00:26:57.034
-Hey.
-Did I scare you?

503
00:26:57.117 --> 00:27:00.245
You snuck up on a woman
in a parking lot at night.

504
00:27:01.622 --> 00:27:03.665
Yeah, Roy, well done.

505
00:27:03.749 --> 00:27:06.793
I'm sorry. I'm an idiot.
I was also an idiot yesterday, so...

506
00:27:07.920 --> 00:27:08.921
It's okay.

507
00:27:14.426 --> 00:27:15.427
Good night, Keeley.

508
00:27:17.638 --> 00:27:18.639
Good night, Roy.

509
00:27:20.057 --> 00:27:22.518
<i>I look back at everything
we've been through,</i>

510
00:27:23.310 --> 00:27:25.229
and I wouldn't change a single thing.

511
00:27:27.272 --> 00:27:28.273
Even now.

512
00:27:30.317 --> 00:27:31.527
What are you saying?

513
00:27:32.611 --> 00:27:35.781
Michelle, if there is something
I could... do

514
00:27:35.864 --> 00:27:39.493
or something I could say
that would make you be happy...

515
00:27:40.577 --> 00:27:42.079
just being with me, I'd do it.

516
00:27:42.663 --> 00:27:44.373
I'd do it in a nanosecond.

517
00:27:44.456 --> 00:27:46.625
But I ain't got no control
over any of that.

518
00:27:48.919 --> 00:27:50.671
You don't have to keep trying anymore.

519
00:27:52.172 --> 00:27:53.173
It's okay.

520
00:27:54.800 --> 00:27:57.803
I'm gonna be okay. Yeah?

521
00:28:05.561 --> 00:28:07.354
Okay, quick feet. There we go.

522
00:28:07.437 --> 00:28:08.438
Shoot.

523
00:28:10.274 --> 00:28:13.360
I promised myself
I would never quit anything in my life.

524
00:28:14.069 --> 00:28:15.487
But you're not quitting, Ted.

525
00:28:17.698 --> 00:28:19.366
You're just letting me go.

526
00:28:23.912 --> 00:28:24.913
Yeah.

527
00:28:25.497 --> 00:28:26.498
Come on.

528
00:28:31.044 --> 00:28:32.045
You ready?

529
00:28:32.129 --> 00:28:33.505
-Yeah.
-Yes. Thank you.

530
00:28:33.589 --> 00:28:35.799
-It's all right.
-I appreciate you, Shannon. Thank you.

531
00:28:35.883 --> 00:28:39.553
Hey, buddy. I'm gonna see you
the second after the season's over, okay?

532
00:28:39.636 --> 00:28:41.346
And we're gonna talk every day?

533
00:28:41.430 --> 00:28:43.932
Absolutely. Just like we do, big guy.
You know it. Okay?

534
00:28:44.016 --> 00:28:46.310
Well, gimme a hug, please. Yeah.

535
00:28:49.563 --> 00:28:51.607
Okay now, okay.

536
00:28:52.274 --> 00:28:55.402
Hey, I love you. Go ahead, get on.

537
00:29:59.883 --> 00:30:02.886
Oi, wanker. Good job tonight.

538
00:30:04.388 --> 00:30:05.722
Thank you, sir.

539
00:30:05.806 --> 00:30:08.433
Keep an eye on us.
We might be turning this thing around.

